Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:55:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Teachers and admins land in the editor after signing in;
 roles are read tidily

Signing in at /missions (by password or Google) now takes a teacher or admin
to the editor, their dashboard; students and guests stay on the missions
page. Arriving already signed in (the Missions link) still shows the
teacher's missions page. The marketing page's log-in buttons take a
signed-in teacher to the editor too.

A role typed by hand as "Teacher" or with a space was refused by the editor,
which compares roles exactly. The User model now reads and stores roles
trimmed and lower-case, and qbl:user checks --role like qbl:update-role does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
